# Independent Affected Review: 7a N15 fig-08 RECOVERY1

Decision: `FIGURE_AFFECTED_PASS_PENDING_RECORD`.

This decision accepts a neutral modern representation for the specific named-point position/order explanation. It does not reconstruct or approve a guessed source A glyph. `A sourceFill = UNKNOWN`; the unknown source bytes have not been recovered, and the original source-fill HOLD remains explicit.

## Independent Observations

- Open 1: original fig-08 PNG. One horizontal right-directed shared line carries A, B, C in that left-to-right order, with A-B wider than B-C. A/B/C are above their markers; a/b/c are below. B is solid; C is visibly a ring. A has a damaged/light diagonal interruption and cannot be reliably classified as solid or open. There is no numerical scale or origin.
- Open 2: current native 640x320 preview. The shared frame, arrow direction, unequal gap order and all six label pairings remain intact. C is visibly a ring. A appears as a short location tick where the two open '+' strokes cross the line; it is non-circular and has no enclosed interior.
- Only the necessary fig-08 prose was extracted from the old authoritative context: it describes A(a) left of B(b), B(b) left of C(c), and the transitivity of the less-than relation. No source exercise was solved, and no answer or choice material was read.

## Judgment

The A marker is suitable here: its position and adjacent A/a labels identify the named point without assigning a source solid/open state. No interval segment, boundary inclusion task, shading, or arithmetic expression gives the '+' an alternative essential meaning in this figure. This acceptance is purpose-specific and must not be generalized to included/excluded interval endpoints.

C is correctly repaired in the actual candidate, not merely in its proposal: the SVG node uses an ink stroke and opaque paper fill, and the observed preview is hollow.

All three locations remain in one deterministic shared frame. The key point-on-line, displacement and collinearity assertions cover all three points within the mapped source group. Layout distances are not numerical source givens. No origin, values, solved-exercise annotation or cultural text was introduced.

At the observed normal width 640, the six Latin labels are legible and correctly associated; no collision, clipping, missing marker or broken raster was observed. The bound native render report records a 22px minimum against 16px, no collisions and no display failures. This is not a new lesson/product-surface acceptance.

No essential defect was found in this affected scope. The independent pixel/prose judgment, not the author rationale or native PASS, supports the decision.

